NEARS-3062 QA — regression-candidate live confirmation (pre-existing, not a
new regression introduced by this refactor).

Observed while typing "Nears Mart" into the Admin search box character by
character (per-keystroke live search UI) — the first keystroke ("N" alone)
fired its own POST /admin/search-routing request that returned HTTP 500.

Admin/storage/logs/laravel.log:
[2026-09-05 15:45:22] production.ERROR: [FAIL] Allowed memory size of
134217728 bytes exhausted (tried to allocate 20480 bytes)
{"trace_id":"402532fb0392d6e2151b676db9bc86b5",
 "correlation_id":"f7550f61-af68-433a-a1a0-a2bc5f8f6b3b",
 "type":"Symfony\\Component\\ErrorHandler\\Error\\FatalError",
 "endpoint":"/admin/search-routing"}

Root cause: a 1-character wildcard keyword (e.g. "N") makes every
`WHERE name/description LIKE '%N%'` query match nearly the entire table —
in this seed DB, Item::where(name LIKE %N% OR description LIKE %N%)->get()
against 14,614 items returns most of the table, then gets cross-joined
against every matching admin route in collectMatches(), exhausting the
128MB PHP memory_limit in a single request.

Confirmed PRE-EXISTING (not introduced by NEARS-3062): the identical query
shape exists byte-for-byte in the pre-refactor controller at commit
97fe75da3 (Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Admin/SearchRoutingController.php
line ~1071-1076):
  $Items = Item::when(...)->where(function ($query) use ($searchKeyword) {
      $query->where('name', 'LIKE', '%' . $searchKeyword . '%')
          ->orWhere('description', 'LIKE', '%' . $searchKeyword . '%');
  })->get();
— same unbounded ->get() with no LIMIT/pagination, same per-model repetition
across ~15 definitions. This refactor moved the logic verbatim; it did not
introduce or worsen this behavior.

Re-verified NOT reproducible with normal-length keywords: subsequent clean
single-shot curl tests with 4+ character keywords, including a broad one
("Test", 1984 results) all returned HTTP 200 without memory exhaustion.
Only extreme 1-2 character wildcards on this ~15k-row Item table trigger it.

Recommendation to conductor/PO: file as a separate, non-blocking
performance Bug (low/medium severity, pre-existing) — e.g. add a minimum
keyword length guard or a query LIMIT — not in scope for NEARS-3062.
